# ── never publish ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# ── test rig ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 13 MB of jsdom and its dependency tree. The suites themselves
# (tests/*.mjs) DO belong in the repo — they are the only proof any
# of this works. Their node_modules does not.
tests/node_modules/
tests/package-lock.json

# ── sprite sources ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Deltarune/Calamity/Terraria/Undertale rips exist only so tiles and
# frames can be cropped out of them. The crops ship; the sources do
# not. js/data/sheets.js keeps the manifest (NEU.sheetSources) and
# tests/fixes14.mjs §5 asserts no shipped module points at one.
img/act4/*/sr-*.png

# ── the documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ADDED 2026-08-17. This site is a puzzle game and memory/story.md is
# the complete walkthrough of it, start to finish, in plain prose.
# Publishing it was never a decision — memory/ simply sat inside site/
# and the mirror took everything. Anyone who found the repo (it is
# named after the site) got the answers before the questions.
#
# Also excluded for the same reason: chain.md (all 45 objectives in
# order), plan-act4.md (every room and boss), build-notes.md (how each
# mechanic works). And workflow.md, which is deploy and DNS detail
# that has no business being served to strangers.
#
# WHY THE WHOLE FOLDER AND NOT A LIST. The four files above are the
# spoilers today. A rule that names four files is a rule that goes
# stale the first time someone writes a fifth, and the failure is
# silent. Excluding the folder and re-including by exception is the
# direction where mistakes are safe.
#
# THE COST, WHICH IS REAL: memory/ is now local-only. The Pages repo
# was the only off-machine copy of 3,600 lines of design documentation
# and it no longer is. That is a backup question, not a publishing
# question, and it needs a separate answer — see memory/pending.md.
#
# TO REVERT: delete the two lines below. Nothing else depends on it;
# no shipped file references memory/ (asserted by fixes17).
memory/
!memory/.gitkeep

# ── the agent instructions and the well-known note (LOCAL ONLY) ──
# ADDED 2026-08-19. Neu's call: every .md on this machine is a working
# doc and stays out of the public repo. CLAUDE.md is the agent brief
# (memory index, house rules, deploy notes) — useful locally, noise
# publicly. README.md is the run/test/deploy doc — same reason. The
# .well-known/discord file itself still ships — that one is a public
# token by design.
CLAUDE.md
README.md
.well-known/README.md

# ── build artefacts / experiments ────────────────────────────────
index-standalone.html
*-standalone.html
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── one-off tool output ──────────────────────────────────────────
# contact-sheet.mjs and pad-sheet.mjs write here. Nothing in _scripts
# ships anyway (it is outside site/), but a .orig backup left next to
# a sprite by mistake would.
*.orig
